Robert F. Kennedy Jr.
Robert F. Kennedy Jr. is an environmental lawyer and political activist based in California who currently serves as Secretary of Health and Human Services under President Donald Trump. He ran for president in 2024, initially seeking the Democratic nomination before launching an independent campaign, suspending it in August 2024, and endorsing Trump.[230] Speculation about a 2028 campaign began as early as July 2025, when Kennedy's super PAC co-hosted an organizing call for supporters that attendees described as a step toward another presidential run.[231] In August 2025, Kennedy denied the speculation on X, framing the statement explicitly as an expression of loyalty to Trump rather than a firm personal decision,[232] and his wife, actress Cheryl Hines, echoed the denial in December 2025.[233] Despite these denials, Kennedy has continued to be widely speculated upon as a 2028 contender, appearing on The Washington Post's ranking of potential 2028 Republican candidates[234] and listed by Ballotpedia among politicians discussed in media as potential 2028 candidates.[235] New York magazine also examined the prospects of a Kennedy run in a dedicated analysis.[236] His cousin, congressional candidate Jack Schlossberg, stated in March 2026 that Kennedy would "definitely" run, citing his following among supporters of the Make America Healthy Again movement.[237]

